{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1535209-are-shields-underpowered","id":1535209,"title":"Are shields underpowered?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-06T22:34:33-07:00","id":1535209,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Are shields underpowered?","content":"Hey all, I was wondering if anyone else always feels that shields are underpowered?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-07T03:18:42-07:00","id":1535212,"title":"","content":"It's a topic that was debated, a lot, in older threads. While not universal? The short answer is yes.<br /> <br /> Though this ranges a lot from &quot;underpowered but that's good actually,&quot; to, &quot;underpowered but no enough to care,&quot; to a half dozen different reasons to dislike how they're implemented based on what people want out of them, to &quot;completely and need a full redo.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-07T13:32:04-07:00","id":1535228,"title":"","content":"The thorn of it IMO is that holding just one sword and having nothing in your empty hand is so valueless. Dual-wielding and two-handers get away with being a +2 to a specific roll that only a minority of combatants will even care about, but the most obvious equivalent for Shields (+1 Defense) is both much broader than clashes and snaps the combat engine's math in half. &quot;+1 Defense while X&quot; might work but is still a risky proposition.<br /> <br /> So the trick is either finding a similarly niche roll that +2 to would still fit the shield-wielder power fantasy, or making having an empty hand more valuable to one-sword-guy, which means that shields, dual wielding, and two-handers can all be a little stronger as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/396-mr-rage","name":"Mr Rage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-07T14:45:27-07:00","id":1535232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Rage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1535209-are-shields-underpowered?p=1535228#post1535228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the trick is either finding a similarly niche roll that +2 to would still fit the shield-wielder power fantasy</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't what the Shield tag does already fit that parameter?<br /> <br /> I mean, apart from the fact that it actually means having +3 to Parry in addition to one other action that isn't an attack?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-07T19:22:38-07:00","id":1535238,"title":"","content":"Shields try to fit that parameter, but do so in a very unsatisfying way.<br /> <br /> First, the Shield tag gives you a +1 net Defense (+2 from Full Defense, -1 from Flurry) bonus for 1i and a -3 dice penalty if the other action is rolled. The other action might add more Initiative or Defense costs on top of it.<br /> <br /> The additional +1 is because you're using a medium weapon with the Shield tag, because that's the only way to get to a net +2. The Shield tag on a light or heavy weapon is worse than just having a medium weapon in one of your hands (even if you're not using it for attacks).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T02:37:57-07:00","id":1535549,"title":"","content":"I think there\u2019s some annoying negative synergy with swords and shields but overall, I\u2019m not too worried about mundane shields.<br /> <br /> What does concern me a little is if the -2 damage of the shield tag scares people off using Thunderbolt Shields in favour of other medium artifact weapons. I could see that going either way as a shield lends itself to a different set of evocations than a daiklave or grimcleaver (fulfilling roles of weapon, mobile cover and armour) but there\u2019s nothing preventing someone from forcing a square peg into a round hole to avoid a small penalty.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T05:14:05-07:00","id":1535554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1535209-are-shields-underpowered?p=1535549#post1535549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> there\u2019s nothing preventing someone from forcing a square peg into a round hole to avoid a small penalty.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to me to be a very self-created problem, I don't think design needs to be concerned with addressing it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T05:18:08-07:00","id":1535555,"title":"","content":"It's not exactly a difficult peg to get into the hole regardless of shapes. Using weapons defensively has been around since we've been using weapons. Having a seemingly matched set of daiklaives, one with Evocations of offense/etc and one of defense is not hard to find inspiration for. It's hardly &quot;forced.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T05:23:41-07:00","id":1535556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1535209-are-shields-underpowered?p=1535554#post1535554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems to me to be a very self-created problem, I don't think design needs to be concerned with addressing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Lioness's phrasing might not be the best design goal, ultimately Exalted designs should be concerned with making sure however you flavor your character's iconic regalia, it's fun to use those items as they are narratively intended to be used. Someone that wants to have an iconic shield should get something out of the Shield tag that's actually making that defensive statement about their character fun. Making shields blatantly sub-optimal puts a big damper on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T02:56:43-07:00","id":1535621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1535209-are-shields-underpowered?p=1535555#post1535555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not exactly a difficult peg to get into the hole regardless of shapes. Using weapons defensively has been around since we've been using weapons. Having a seemingly matched set of daiklaives, one with Evocations of offense/etc and one of defense is not hard to find inspiration for. It's hardly &quot;forced.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a secondary defensive daklave having evocations where it functions like armour or cover (examples I specifically gave) seems like it might be a bit forced. I think it's worth questioning what extent the Daiklave of Defending is a real thing outside of forum discussions like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 05-15-2024, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T05:51:27-07:00","id":1535636,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem is that the &quot;shape&quot; of an Artifact is rarely that important to the Evocations it gets. If I want to have blue jade diaklaives that are themed around creating ice in combat to aid me, it's not like it would inherently be better to use some other form of weapon. Goremauls aren't somehow more aligned to making ice walls that act as cover, and grimcleavers aren't inherently better for summoning ice to perform a magical grapple.<br /> <br /> The only thing that strikes me as particularly &quot;forum theory craft&quot; is bothering at all since most native Charm sets have robust defense boosters that make wasting Evocations on such tricks instead of more niche effects that you can't get in your native Charms something people aren't going to do. Getting armor especially is kinda silly because you can just wear armor, get Resistance Charms (usually) to grant you Armor, or take a certain spell with TCS; and armor doesn't stack by default.<br /> <br /> It also feels verging on a strawman to treat the &quot;Daiklaive of Defending&quot; as just a bunch of basic defense boosters instead of a properly themed Artifact that has appropriately matching effects that are also focused on defense broadly. If people didn't want an off-hand defense boosting Artifact weapon... they wouldn't want Thunderbolt Shields even if the Shield tag itself was considering neutral/good instead of questionable (at best).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T08:36:18-07:00","id":1535642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1535209-are-shields-underpowered?p=1535636#post1535636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem is that the &quot;shape&quot; of an Artifact is rarely that important to the Evocations it gets. If I want to have blue jade diaklaives that are themed around creating ice in combat to aid me, it's not like it would inherently be better to use some other form of weapon. Goremauls aren't somehow more aligned to making ice walls that act as cover, and grimcleavers aren't inherently better for summoning ice to perform a magical grapple.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if this is consistent with how Artifacts have been designed thus far*.<br /> <br /> Sure, there's nothing stopping a person from homebrewing their weapons with Evocations of a kind were the weapon form is completely arbitrary, but I greatly doubt that any of the other weapon tags are attractive enough by themselves to make them worth distinguishing on that front.<br /> <br /> Assuming there are any distinctions at all. Daiklaves and Reaper Daiklaves are mechanically identical in the base weapon form, so the only real question for their Evocations is &quot;does this fit the vibe of whether or not it's a fantasy katana&quot;. Stormcaller is a Reaper Daiklave primarily to fit aesthetically with the notion that you'll constantly be sheathing it in between attacks.<br /> <br /> The idea that a Thunderbolt Shield has no call to go for Evocations that are Evocative of shields in some fashion strikes me as not particularly compelling even if the Shield tag <i>did</i> do something more.<br /> <br /> * And if it is, I would think that the design trend that would make a lot more sense to call for would be &quot;make Evocations more consistently aligned with the weapon they grow out of&quot; than &quot;make Evocations do whatever and double down on the idea that these weapons are distinguished and made most attractive by their Tags&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T15:09:41-07:00","id":1535682,"title":"","content":"I don't really think that makes your case.<br /> <br /> Stormcaller isn't, by your own logic, a Reaper Daiklave because it's important for Stormcaller to have the mechanical functions of a slashing sword, but purely for the invocation of a cultural element from the real world. While the weapon form might not be strictly arbitrary, it's divorced from the practical shape in favor of fulfilling a fantasy. Slings are not inherently good at killing large creatures. There's nothing special about slings for slaying giants. But we have an example sling for killing Behemoths in the books to invoke the David vs. Goliath story. If the designers wanted to focus on Hercules as an archer (something that's a bit less popular, but still part of mythology to draw from) you could easily have the same Artifact as a bow instead.<br /> <br /> The arbitrary aspect is which myths and fantasies you pick for your design. If I'm making an Artifact that my War focused character lofts high to inspire troops as it's central premise, choosing between a normal Daiklave (ex: Joan of Arc), a Reaper Daiklave (ex: Napoleon), or even a Grand Daiklaive (ex: William Wallace) is, yes, arbitrary... but they're all equally valid choices to base my Artifact around.<br /> <br /> Mythology and such sources of inspiration are also messy. The Aegis is probably one of the more iconic mythological shields. But the attributes assigned to it don't really care about being a shield (mostly it scares and demoralizes people), and even in mythology it's been a shield, a breastplate, or just a collection of special items integrated into a goat hide that can be waved around as a banner or attached to a shield/armor/over clothing.<br /> <br /> When we get into actual design trends in the books, the farther away from obvious cultural inspirations, the more arbitrary the specific stat blocks get. While an Artifact that's focused on turning blood into sorcerous motes needs to do Lethal damage, why does it need to be a giant axe? Would anything be lost if it was pretty much any other weapon? <br /> <br /> I'm not actually claiming that &quot;a Thunderbolt Shield has no call to go for Evocations that are Evocative of shields in some fashion.&quot; I'm claiming that &quot;in some fashion,&quot; is so broad that it renders the specific stat block moot because you can find evocative inspirations for so many other options among the list. There's so much inspirational overlap out there that it's exceedingly hard to say there's anything that is unique to any given Artifact stat block:a Thunderbolt Shield, Artifact Breastplate, and a Grand Daiklave, should all have Evocations that evoke those forms... but those can also all be the same exact set of Evocations at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-22T12:23:00-07:00","id":1536110,"title":"","content":"Shields in Exalted are just not inherently better at <i>being shields</i> than other, better weapons.<br /> <br /> As a tangent, this reminds me of how in Ars Magica, when you create magic items, things do have associated bonuses based on their Shape.<br /> For example, a dagger is better at damaging effects than a bandage. You're not punished for making a bandage that wounds, it's just easier to make a dagger do that and the effect would be stronger or at least enchanting it would probably be faster.<br /> <br /> Exalted doesn't have that, beyond the Magical Materials themselves, but that's just the material of the artifact - not its shape.<br /> <br /> So, you could pick up a Thunderbolt Shield orrrrr you could just make a Daiklave or Dire Chain or whatever other Medium Artifact weapon you want and give it Parry-enhancing Evocations and effects - and you could do that without sacrificing other Evocations that enhance things like damage, attacks, create magical attacks and have other utility effects as well.<br /> True, you could make an artifact shield that does all (or most) of that - but the fact is that any other weapon can do the same exact things <b>while also</b> not gimping your damage output and having other advantages (higher Overwhelming for Daiklave, a host of tags for Dire Chain, Lethal damage and so on).<br /> <br /> Shields may not be bad in a vacuum (if a hypothetical exalt finds herself in an empty cave with nothing but a shield lying around, she couldn't go wrong with picking up the shield), they're just bad when compared with literally every other weapon because every other weapon can do what they do PLUS extra.<br /> <br /> Also, unless I missed some errata, shields don't actually give you any bonus to Parry - beyond the base bonus that all Medium weapons get, that is. The Shield tag just lets you put Full Defense in a flurry while permanently reducing the weapon's damage by 2.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why the Shield tag doesn't do just <i>a little</i> something extra like give you or another character Cover (even Light Cover). I guess you could do that with a Stunt, but that's like saying <i>&quot;it's fine because at </i><b>my </b>table <i>it is</i><i>... </i><b>My </b>storyteller<i> lets us...&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I chalk it up to the bitter taste left by the previous edition's inherent problem with devolving into &quot;unstoppable force vs immovable object&quot; death spiral.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-22T15:14:06-07:00","id":1536118,"title":"","content":"I think it goes farther back. early development and early 1e clearly wanted to regulate shields to the same place as helmets: realistically things of value such that nameless mooks would clearly want them, but beneath the epic grandeur of the Exalted to have to care about beyond being character quirks. Shields and helmets were just ways to code different military forces to real world inspirations. IME the folks that wanted Exalted to emphasize the Sword and Sandals side of the game a bit more than the Wuxia side of the game (which was generally sold as the default style of the game to people getting into it, and it still holds a strong &quot;anime&quot; RPG reputation despite all the non-anime and non-wuxia stuff in it) pushed for better sword &amp; board mechanical representation to balance out all the fancy MA weapons. So they got put into 1e a bit awkwardly, and neither 2e or 3e really tried to find a &quot;place&quot; in the game for shields despite including them because at least enough players wanted mechanically significant ones to make it valuable to include them.<br /> <br /> I think one of the best facts in support of this is that 3e has a &quot;shield&quot; tag to begin with. We don't have &quot;sword&quot; or &quot;axe&quot; or &quot;spear&quot; or &quot;bow,&quot; as tags. We have common tags that most swords have, etc. so you can look at a set of tags and guess what kind of weapon it is with decent accuracy. Flame is pretty much the only other tag that's so closely linked to a specific type of weapon (and even then it's actual mechanics could be justified on weapons that don't actually use firedust flame bursts). Instead of having ~3 defense focused Tags and any shields being identifiable by being loaded up with a decent number of them like every other weapon stat block, shields are tautologically linked to a tag. In past threads I've always been proponent of splitting the Shield tag up into multiple tags. One tag is trying to define a gigantic class of combat implements, and it doesn't work in a satisfactory way. Instead of shields emerging from the combat and equipment rules naturally, 3e is still just stuffing them in because people want shields on some level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T04:42:15-07:00","id":1536337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1535209-are-shields-underpowered?p=1536110#post1536110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, unless I missed some errata, shields don't actually give you any bonus to Parry - beyond the base bonus that all Medium weapons get, that is. The Shield tag just lets you put Full Defense in a flurry while permanently reducing the weapon's damage by 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is if shields had a higher parry than other medium weapons that would make them the best equipment option in the game, achieving a resting parry of 8 through a resources purchase would be more significant than most artifact weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T16:05:21-07:00","id":1536388,"title":"","content":"But Serpent Axis didn't call for a boost to Parry.<br /> <br /> In the numerous previous threads about this, both people that want to make shields better and people that don't think it's worth changing all agree than a flat +1 Parry addition (at least for personal use, maybe not for BGs) would be bad for the current combat math.<br /> <br /> There are lots of things you can do besides that:<br /> <br /> - Make the Shield tag more appealing by getting rid of a damage penalty and/or negating the Defense penalty during the flurry (making the shield tag functional for everything but mundane heavy weapons).<br /> - Improve Defend Other's bonus to the person you're covering.<br /> - Negate the Flexible Tag.<br /> - Provide Cover in some fashion<br /> - Gain a Clash bonus<br /> etc.<br /> <br /> There's a lot you can do to make shields feel better at being shields without just increasing resting Parry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}